# Data files are bytes, not text.
#
# Verbatim memorization is measured character by character, so a line-ending
# conversion is a change of the thing being measured. Git on Windows converts
# LF to CRLF on checkout by default (core.autocrlf=true), and that is exactly
# how the canon freeze of 2026-08-10 came to hold Windows line endings while
# the published files, and every corpus a model was trained on, hold Unix ones.
# See AMENDMENT_2_LINE_ENDINGS.md.
#
# This protects our own repository. It cannot protect a clone of somebody
# else's — which is where the damage came from — so the authority on dataset
# bytes is src/fetch_data.py and the hashes in the registry, never a checkout.
*.csv   -text
*.jsonl -text
